<h1>Endpoints file</h1>
<p>The AI agent has to know which machines exist and how to address them. That knowledge lives in the
  controller. The Endpoints panel is where a team registers its machines and checks that each one
  answers. The panel's <strong>Save</strong> button writes them to a JSON file, by default in the
  <code>Endpoints</code> folder of the controller's working directory. Register the machines, save,
  and put the file in the run folder for the AI agent.</p>

<h2 id="file">File format</h2>
{{ codeblock.block('{
  "endpoints": [
    {
      "type": "Host Name",
      "host_name": "lab-linux-1",
      "ip": "10.0.0.21",
      "resolved_hostname": "lab-linux-1",
      "port": 50051,
      "secure_enabled": true,
      "os_name": "Linux 6.8.0-45-generic",
      "version": "0.1.0",
      "accepted_duplicates": []
    },
    {
      "type": "IP",
      "host_name": "",
      "ip": "10.0.0.31",
      "resolved_hostname": "lab-win-1",
      "port": 50051,
      "secure_enabled": true,
      "os_name": "Windows 11",
      "version": "0.1.0",
      "accepted_duplicates": []
    }
  ]
}', "json") }}

<p>Each entry is one registered machine. <code>type</code> is <code>"Host Name"</code> or
  <code>"IP"</code>, depending on how the machine was added. A machine added by IP address has an empty
  <code>host_name</code>, and <code>resolved_hostname</code> carries the name the controller found for
  the address. <code>os_name</code> is the operating system the machine reported the last time it
  answered, such as <code>Windows 11</code>, <code>Linux 6.8.0-45-generic</code> or
  <code>macOS 15.1</code>, and <code>version</code> is the Orcraft version installed on it. Both are
  empty for a machine that has not answered yet.</p>
<p>The value the AI agent puts in an endpoint field is the <code>host_name</code>, or the
  <code>ip</code> for a machine added by address, followed by <code>:port</code> when the port is not
  the default <code>50051</code>. A request that names a machine by host name, by address or by
  operating system resolves through these fields.</p>

<h2 id="loading">Loading into a controller</h2>
<p>The same file loads back into any controller through the panel's <strong>Load</strong> button. One
  saved list therefore serves the team and its AI agents alike, and it is the only list of machines
  the AI agent works from.</p>
